(A list returned from a parameter is the caller's own copy: returning a
 freed list gives an empty list that takes appends.)
To 'give back' with a list called items.
  Return a list, items.

a list called xs is ["a"].
Free xs.
a list called back is 'give back' of xs.
append "d" to back.
On error print "append to the returned copy refused".
Print "back: {back}".
